  "pull_request": {
    "number": 170,
    "title": "Refactor/clean up dylint wrapper error handling",
    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR cleans up error handling in the Dylint wrapper by replacing panic-based execution with explicit error handling and clearer user-facing error messages.\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n\r\n* Refactored configuration loading to handle file read and TOML parsing errors using explicit `match` expressions.\r\n* Improved `cargo dylint` execution by replacing `expect()` with graceful error handling and appropriate exit codes.\r\n* Preserved existing behavior while making failures easier to understand and debug.\r\n* Continued to respect `.lintignore` during execution.\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\n\r\n* ✅ `cargo fmt`\r\n* ✅ `cargo build`\r\n* ✅ `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\r\n\r\n> Note: The existing UI test failure is unrelated to this refactor and is caused by pre-existing UI test state rather than the Dylint wrapper changes introduced in this PR.\r\n\r\n**Closes #67**\r\n",
