        "author_association": "MEMBER",
        "body": " Hi @ASIDISG, Thanks for your contribution! 🙌\r\n  \r\n  It looks like the CI tests are failing because of a small syntax error in cargo-cost-lint/src/main.rs. The Rust compiler is reporting an \"unclosed delimiter\" (a missing or extra curly brace { / }).\r\n  \r\n  Specifically, it looks like an if block around line 138 (if !lint_flags.is_empty() {) is missing its closing brace }, which is causing the compiler to get confused when it reaches the end of the main() function at line 315.          \r\n  \r\n  If you are using an IDE like VS Code or RustRover with rust-analyzer enabled, it should highlight the exact location with a red squiggle. You can also run this locally to find it:\r\n  \r\n    cargo check -p cargo-cost-lint\r\n  \r\n  Could you double-check your braces in that file and push a fix? Let me know if you need any help finding it!***\r\n"
      },
